    "text": "Consider a hydrogen atom with its electron in the <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></mrow></msup></math> orbital. An electromagnetic radiation of wavelength 90 nm is used to ionize the atom. If the kinetic energy of the ejected electron is 10.4 eV, then the value of n is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1242</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
    "image": null
  },
